                  "op": "undecidable",
                  "reason": "environment-visibility-gap",
                  "needed": "whether the ingress-nginx strict-validate-path-type configuration option is enabled"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "consequence": {
        "kind": "workload-failure",
        "exposedClass": "action-required",
        "statement": "With ingress-nginx strict-validate-path-type enabled (the default in ingress-nginx >= 1.12.0), the validate.nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io admission webhook rejects the HTTP01 challenge Ingress because its path contains a dot. The controller then logs 'Error presenting challenge: admission webhook ... denied the request', and the HTTP01 challenge cannot be solved.",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      "statement": "cert-manager 1.18.0 creates ACME HTTP01 challenge Ingress routes with PathType Exact. ingress-nginx's strict-validate-path-type option (available from 1.8.0 and on by default from 1.12.0) rejects these routes, so presenting the challenge fails with an admission webhook denial."
    },
